_model: definition
---
title: Definition 1
---
order: 1
---
short_label: X.Def.III.1
---
statement: Given a rational straight line and an apotome, if the square on the whole is greater than the square on the annex by the square on a straight line commensurable in length with the whole, and the whole is commensurable in length with the rational line set out, let the apotome be called a <i>first apotome.</i>
---
group: defX.III
---
subsection: III
---
body:

